<td id="A4.T5.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T5.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">*</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Statistical tests on absolute slope values. Mean <math id="A4.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\beta}|=0.0573" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0573</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\beta}|=0.0573</annotation></semantics></math>. Significance levels: * <math id="A4.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, ** <math id="A4.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Expt P3.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each step <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we performed the following steps:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Karma change: <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x_{i}(t)=x_{i}(t)-x_{i}(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x_{i}(t)=x_{i}(t)-x_{i}(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2. Mean neighbor karma at <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{x}_{N(i)}(t-1)=\frac{1}{|N(i)|}\sum_{j\in N(i)}x_{j}(t-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{x}_{N(i)}(t-1)=\frac{1}{|N(i)|}\sum_{j\in N(i)}x_{j}(t-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Neighbors are derived from the one-hop ego-network neighbors from the reply graph. Isolated agents are excluded.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3. OLS regression with the equation <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta x_{i}(t)\sim\hat{\beta}(t)\cdot\bar{x}_{N(i)}(t-1)+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta x_{i}(t)\sim\hat{\beta}(t)\cdot\bar{x}_{N(i)}(t-1)+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> measures how strongly the <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> neighbor karma predicts <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> change.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Non-zero, time varying slopes (<math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>) indicate that the reply graph transmit engagement signals across agents, establishing the graph-to-agent state portion of co-evolution. Since the graph itself is, by construction, endogenously formed by reply-driven interactions (agent-state-to-graph), these two portions together close the co-evolutionary loop: agent states shape the network, the network then shapes future agent states.
This is consistent with studies of network-mediated influence changes of co-evolution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ D.3 Expt P3. ‣ Appendix D MoltBook as an example of MASS ‣ Social Theory Should Be a Structural Prior for Agentic AI: A Formal Framework for Multi-Agent Social Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 6</span></a>shows the results where we test whether the OLS slopes <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> have a non-zero magnitude. This slope measures the difference between the neighbor’s karma at <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> and the agent’s karma change at <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Having a non-zero magnitude indicates that the reply network <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> transmits engagement signals regardless of direction. Since the slopes oscillate in sign, the test is performed on <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\beta}(t)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\beta}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math> rather than the signed <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T6" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Test</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Statistic</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">p-value</span></th>
<th id="A4.T6.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T6.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sig</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T6.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Wilcoxon signed-rank on <math id="A4.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\text{slope}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>slope</mtext><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\text{slope}|</annotation></semantics></math> (one-tailed greater)</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A4.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=36.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">W</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">36.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=36.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.0039</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T6.2.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">**</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T6.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">One-sample <math id="A4.T6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-test on <math id="A4.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\text{slope}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>slope</mtext><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\text{slope}|</annotation></semantics></math> vs. 0 (one-tailed)</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="A4.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=2.289" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2.289</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=2.289</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.0257</span></td>
<td id="A4.T6.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A4.T6.2.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">*</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Statistical tests on absolute slope values. Mean <math id="A4.T6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\hat{\beta}|=0.0573" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0573</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\hat{\beta}|=0.0573</annotation></semantics></math>. Significance levels: * <math id="A4.T6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, ** <math id="A4.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The observation of non-zero and time-varying slopes indicate that the reply network structure is predictive of individual karma change, consistent with network-mediated influence changes of co-evolution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For completeness, <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ D.3 Expt P3. ‣ Appendix D MoltBook as an example of MASS ‣ Social Theory Should Be a Structural Prior for Agentic AI: A Formal Framework for Multi-Agent Social Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 7</span></a> tests for directional bias and trend of the <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> coefficient. The signed slopes alternate in direction (fraction positive = 0.44), indicating bidirectional coupling, that is, there exist both positive and negative influence days, rather than a unidirectional trend, consistent with the mutual co-evolution claim.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Test</span></th>
