<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Statistical tests on slope estimates <math id="A4.T7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\beta}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\beta}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Summary statistics: mean <math id="A4.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=-0.0033" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0033</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=-0.0033</annotation></semantics></math>, median <math id="A4.T7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0.0000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0.0000</annotation></semantics></math>, fraction positive <math id="A4.T7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0.44" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.44</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0.44</annotation></semantics></math>. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Expt P4.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We computed the Wasserstein-1 distance between the distributions of log-transformed agent karma across time. We used the scipy.stats.wasserstein_distance implementation.
Specifically, we calculated:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}(t)=W_{1}\!\bigl(p_{t-1},\,p_{t}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}(t)=W_{1}\!\bigl(p_{t-1},\,p_{t}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results show non-zero and time-varying <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> which indicates endogenous distributional shift driven by interaction dynamics rather than a fixed external data distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ D.4 Expt P4. ‣ Appendix D MoltBook as an example of MASS ‣ Social Theory Should Be a Structural Prior for Agentic AI: A Formal Framework for Multi-Agent Social Systems" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 8</span></a>tests whether the 9 Wasserstein-1 distances (i.e., one distance for each time step) are all significantly greater than zero, which means whether the overall karma distribution shifted across the window. All tests confirm that consecutive daily karma distributions are non-stationary (mean <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1}=0.2528" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2528</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1}=0.2528</annotation></semantics></math>). The KS test confirms that the overall distribution has shifted significantly from the first to the last observation day (<math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=0.0456,p=2.5E-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0456</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=0.0456,p=2.5E-3</annotation></semantics></math>). These results are consistend with endogeneous distributional drift driven by agent interactions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Test</span></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T8.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Statistic</span></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T8.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">p-value</span></th>
<th id="A4.T8.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A4.T8.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Sig</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
